ked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable in 4.8 master\n- Reproducable in 4.7.2\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nNot entirely sure when and how this regression was created, very likely something I overlooked in my PR that changed how XR updates the viewport size.\n\nIn PCVR, when rendering the HMD output to the main viewport, the left eye is displayed on screen in the Godot window that opens.\n\nWhen this window is resized, the XR display isn't resized accordingly. It is only sized  correctly on initialisation.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun any of the XR sample projects on a PC, resize the window.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/xr/openxr_character_centric_movement","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124083/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124083/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}